Cycle 500 liveness repair derived from live fail-close evidence.

Observed durable evidence:
- new DevOS admission was fenced after repeated lease-expired/effect-unknown episodes;
- live failure: native_supervisor_idle_maintenance_wait_timeout;
- Browser/fleet transport itself is healthy (7 ACTIVE agents).

Root cause:
NativeSupervisorClient stamps #lastMaintenanceAtMs when maintenance starts. If a maintenance pass lasts longer than maintenanceIntervalMs, its next empty command cycle sees the interval already elapsed and immediately launches another pass before DevOS idle work gets a maintenance-free window. Repetition can starve the existing idle task-cycle lane.

Change:
Stamp the maintenance cooldown in the existing promise finally block, after the pass settles. This guarantees a cooldown window after every long maintenance pass while preserving:
- the existing single command/maintenance scheduler;
- remote command first-admission;
- the existing bounded 15s idle wait;
- no task retry;
- no Browser effect replay;
- no lease or release authority expansion.

Regression asserts cooldown ordering and preserves the existing bounded wait.

No admission reopen, no production promotion, no release/install, and no replay of currently ambiguous/leased work.

